No — `db.js:11-16`'s `withClient` never releases the client if `fn(client)` throws: there's no `try/finally` around `client.release()`. `pool.log` shows `idle=0` at every sample while `waiting` climbs steadily (7→28) — that's connections leaking, not genuine demand. Raising `max` would just delay the same exhaustion.

Fix:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```

