The cause is in `db.js:11-16`: `withClient` calls `client.release()` only after `fn(client)` resolves. If `fn` throws, `release()` never runs and that connection is held forever. Every failing query permanently removes one connection from the pool, so `waiting` grows without bound.

Fix the leak first:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```

Raising `max` would only delay the exhaustion, not stop it.

