const result = await fn(client);
client.release();
```

If `fn(client)` throws, `client.release()` is skipped and that connection is gone from the pool forever. Wrap it in try/finally:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```

