The cause is in `db.js:11-16`:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  const result = await fn(client);
  client.release();
  return result;
}
```

If `fn(client)` throws, `client.release()` on line 14 never runs, so that connection is checked out forever. Over an hour of occasional query errors, the pool fills with orphaned clients and everything else queues behind `waiting`.

Fix by releasing in a `finally`:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```

